text='''#1843: assisted rotating neck stretch

One representative side in a 5 s clip: 2 s entry, 1 s held contact, 2 s return. Exercise_1843 retains the source 20–30 s workout hold and repeat-other-side instruction. The 32° axial head turn is authored for a modest visual demonstration; it is not a medical prescription. The neck/head distribute that turn without a forced lateral neck bend. Head rotation precedes the outside hand approach. The left palm lightly supports the chin; the right palm touches the occiput. Hands stay open and relaxed.

The source leaves furniture and leg placement unspecified. The accepted 1368 floor-seated base is reused: supported pelvis, extended relaxed legs, 11.524° natural knee bend and supported heels. Calves remain free at approximately 7 mm clearance. The complete lower-body transforms are preserved within 1.67e-6 matrix elements, and the complete inherited binding is exact; canonical 10,582 vertices, 21,160 triangles, 51 bones, Basis, rest skeleton, UVs, topology and original source IDs are unchanged. There are no morph targets, new binding fits, body fairing, runtime vertex caches or corrective reset state.

Only the arms/head are new. The inherited thigh-resting arm pose caused actual arm/trunk crossings in this exercise; 1843 starts with hands relaxed outside the thighs. An explicit rear/outside passing arm pose, an outward shoulder arc confined to that transition and a stable anatomical elbow plane remove that crossing without changing the body. Endpoint rigid hand translations are solved against actual chin/scalp skin; no face/head deformation is introduced. Palm contact is an envelope, not a claim that the whole palm is flat against curved skin. Native geometric normals are distinct from the DQ-rotated source NORMAL transport references.

All 151 native and actual Three.js/shared-DQ decoded states pass the scoped floor/support, full-arm/hand/head/neck/trunk and bilateral-leg clearance, positive-area and exact-loop checks. All 51 joints and DQ POSITION/NORMAL references are included. Mandatory game QA reports 0 errors and one canonical mouth/lip back-to-back face pair at frames 30, 75 and 120. The unchanged source faces 2302/1670 are localized in asset-qa.json; deleting canonical mouth geometry is not justified. Actual warnings are retained in asset-qa.json and verification-summary.json. These tests are discrete and do not claim global or continuous collision freedom. Root owns actual GPU natural-motion judgement, muscle fields and camera-width integration.

The two default cameras retain the full body while showing chin/occiput approaches. clip.json separates source muscle labels and hold time from authored staging. source-verification.json and ../../seated-neck/dependency-provenance.json record exact current source/model/runtime hashes. Only curated-files.json entries form the delivery; read-only dependencies stay in their accepted packets.

Reproduce with the existing Blender 5.2.3 executable, -b -t 2 --python-exit-code 1 --factory-startup. Run seated-neck/build.py -- --final, verify_native.py -- --game-qa, export_motion.py, node verify_export.mjs, the system Python check_decoded.py, render_wire.py, inspect_qa.py, then package.py. No paid generation, video, restricted visual derivative, shared runtime edit or Git mutation is used.
'''
